(GOVERNMENT OF INDIA - MINISTRY OF COMMERCE AND INDUSTRY) Tj
T*
(OPERATIONAL GUIDELINES: FUND OF FUNDS FOR STARTUPS \(FFS\) / SIDBI / DPIIT) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Overview & Objective:) Tj
T*
(Rs. 10,000 Crore corpus managed by SIDBI contributing capital to SEBI-) Tj
T*
(registered Alternative Investment Funds \(AIFs\), which invest directly in) Tj
T*
(innovative DPIIT-recognized startups.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Eligibility Criteria:) Tj
T*
(1. Startup must be recognized by DPIIT.) Tj
T*
(2. Must be incorporated as a Private Limited Company.) Tj
T*
(3. Company age must not exceed 10 years from the date of incorporation.) Tj
T*
(4. Startup must demonstrate innovative business model, scalable unit) Tj
T*
(   economics, and technology orientation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Financial Assistance and Subsidy:) Tj
T*
(1. Venture equity and structured growth capital deployed via SIDBI-) Tj
T*
(   partnered Daughter VC Funds \(Series Pre-A, Series A, Series B\).) Tj
T*
(3. Maximum financial assistance cap is Rs 10.00 Crore per unit.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Mandatory Documents Checklist:) Tj
T*
(1. DPIIT Certificate of Recognition) Tj
T*
(2. Certificate of Incorporation and MoA/AoA) Tj
T*
(3. Audited Financial Statements since incorporation) Tj
T*
(4. Cap Table & Dilution history) Tj
T*
(5. Detailed Information Memorandum \(IM\) & Financial Model) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(5. Application Procedure:) Tj
T*
(1. Mode: Direct outreach to SIDBI-empanelled AIFs / Venture Capitalists listed on Startup India) Tj
T*
(2. Official Portal: https://www.startupindia.gov.in/content/sih/en/fund-of-funds-for-startups.html) Tj
T*
ET
